#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161698 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162132 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "130d80d7-d0f9-5979-b966-e6c0bf7a27e9" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Covariance Using the Definition"}] :question/id #uuid "9716c386-896d-5b3b-a0e6-d6d3d1a83cbf" :question/math-academy-id "e-10348" :question/problem "The joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ for the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given below.\n\n| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.1$ | $0.5$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0$ | $0.4$ |\n\nCalculate the covariance of $X$ and $Y.$" :question/worked-solution "The covariance of two discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ with joint support $S$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Cov}[X, Y] = \\sum_{(x,y)\\in S}(x − \\textrm E[X])(y − \\textrm E[Y])f(x,y).\n$$\n\nFirst, let's find the marginal mass functions for $X$ and $Y.$ These are given by the row and column totals, respectively.\n\n| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | $f_X$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.1$ | $0.5$ | $0.6$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0$ | $0.4$ | $0.4$ |\n| $f_Y$ | $0.1$ | $0.9$ | $1$ |\n\nWe now compute $\\textrm{E}[X]$ and $\\textrm{E}[Y],$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\sum }_{x\\in {S}_{X}}x\\cdot {f}_{X}(x) \\\\  & =1\\cdot 0.6+2\\cdot 0.4 \\\\  & =0.6+0.8 \\\\  & =1.4 \\\\ \\text{E}[Y] & ={\\sum }_{y\\in {S}_{Y}}y\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y) \\\\  & =0\\cdot 0.1+1\\cdot 0.9 \\\\  & =0+0.9 \\\\  & =0.9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the formula for the covariance, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}[X,Y] & ={\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}(x-\\text{E}[X])(y-\\text{E}[Y])f(x,y) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}(x-1.4)(y-0.9)f(x,y) \\\\  & =(1-1.4)(0-0.9)f(1,0) \\\\  & +(1-1.4)(1-0.9)f(1,1) \\\\  & +(2-1.4)(0-0.9)f(2,0) \\\\  & +(2-1.4)(1-0.9)f(2,1) \\\\  & =(-0.4)(-0.9)(0.1) \\\\  & +(-0.4)(0.1)(0.5) \\\\  & +(0.6)(-0.9)(0) \\\\  & +(0.6)(0.1)(0.4) \\\\  & =0.04.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161700 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162134 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fab3dcab-d386-5f54-bfba-f2e5951af9ba" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Covariance Given a Joint Probability Density Function"}] :question/id #uuid "ebf98f0c-765c-5cc4-bfa0-89ffefe450f4" :question/math-academy-id "e-10356" :question/problem "The random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability density function\n\n![](images/be/bebcce16140d945e7f9059627d76fc4a28f5638294029c4ccf3ccd0adbfb71a2.svg)\n\nFind the covariance of $X$ and $Y.$" :question/worked-solution "The joint support of $X$ and $Y$ is given by the rectangle \n\n$$\nS = [0,1] \\times [2,3].\n$$\n\nMoreover, we can write \n\n$$\nf(x,y) = g(x) \\cdot h(y),\n$$\n\nwhere $g(x) =\\dfrac{3}{5} \\sqrt{x}$ and $h(y) =y.$ \n\nTherefore, $X$ and $Y$ are independent, and consequently $\\textrm{Cov}[X,Y] = 0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161701 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162135 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b4549d88-dfbd-57e0-a673-99e394563613" :knowledge-point/title "Stating the Covariance Using the Definition"}] :question/id #uuid "5e69ba34-d7f9-512b-9d53-f00f8f556049" :question/math-academy-id "e-10357" :question/problem "The joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ for the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ with joint support $S=S_X\\times S_Y$ is given below.\n\n| $f$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.15$ | $0.25$ |\n| $X=4$ | $0.45$ | $0.15$ |\n\nFind an expression for the covariance in sigma notation." :question/worked-solution "The covariance of two discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ with joint support $S$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Cov}[X, Y] = \\sum_{(x,y)\\in S}(x − \\textrm E[X])(y − \\textrm E[Y])f(x,y).\n$$\n\nFirst, let's find the marginal mass functions for $X$ and $Y.$ These are given by the row and column totals, respectively.\n\n| $f$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=5$ | $f_X$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.15$ | $0.25$ | $0.4$ |\n| $X=4$ | $0.45$ | $0.15$ | $0.6$ |\n| $f_Y$ | $0.6$ | $0.4$ | $1$ |\n\nWe now compute $\\textrm{E}[X]$ and $\\textrm{E}[Y],$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\sum }_{x\\in {S}_{X}}x\\cdot {f}_{X}(x) \\\\  & =1\\cdot 0.4+4\\cdot 0.6 \\\\  & =0.4+2.4 \\\\  & =2.8 \\\\ \\text{E}[Y] & ={\\sum }_{y\\in {S}_{Y}}y\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y) \\\\  & =2\\cdot 0.6+5\\cdot 0.4 \\\\  & =1.2+2 \\\\  & =3.2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the formula for the covariance, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}[X,Y] & ={\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}(x-\\text{E}[X])(y-\\text{E}[Y])f(x,y) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}(x-2.8)(y-3.2)f(x,y).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161702 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162136 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "929a4b02-6c3d-59ce-b774-7ca6487077ff" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Covariance Using the Shortcut Formula"}] :question/id #uuid "08ae7ab0-00d9-51db-9c5d-d3b13ddaedac" :question/math-academy-id "e-10358" :question/problem "The joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ for the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given below.\n\n| $f$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.2$ | $0.2$ |\n| $X=4$ | $0.4$ | $0.2$ |\n\nIf $\\textrm{E} [X]=2.8$ and $\\textrm{E}[Y] = 2.4,$ calculate the covariance of $X$ and $Y.$" :question/worked-solution "The covariance of $X$ and $Y$ can be calculated using the formula\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Cov}[X,Y]\n=\n\\textrm{E} [XY] - \\textrm{E}[X]\\cdot \\textrm{E}[Y].\n$$\n\nWe use the rule of the lazy statistician to find $\\textrm{E}[XY]\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[XY] & ={\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}xy\\cdot f(x,y) \\\\  & =(1)(2)(0.2)+(1)(3)(0.2)+(4)(2)(0.4)+(4)(3)(0.2) \\\\  & =6.6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the covariance formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}[X,Y] & =\\text{E}[XY]-\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y] \\\\  & =6.6-(2.8)(2.4) \\\\  & =-0.12.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162422 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162136 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "929a4b02-6c3d-59ce-b774-7ca6487077ff" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Covariance Using the Shortcut Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "82b061aa-a562-5cec-b12f-b031e6b197d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159735} {:answer/id #uuid "9dc50379-a73f-56f1-a77e-1b9ac7f0f5e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159736} {:answer/id #uuid "bf1e623d-3883-51ff-9be3-842a410c8835" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159737} {:answer/id #uuid "06809080-8efa-5670-a26b-998d5dc4f55a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6.4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159738} {:answer/id #uuid "3b7115c8-ba08-5aac-b629-621bf83dee7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4.8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159739}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3b7115c8-ba08-5aac-b629-621bf83dee7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4.8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159739} :answer-field/id #uuid "b1eacff7-d507-52b8-80a6-7de096999f8b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159734}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e37b553f-54ac-5d84-b352-476c36a3f396" :question/math-academy-id "q-146149" :question/problem "If $\\text{E}[X]=20,$ $\\text{E}[Y]=2,$ and $\\text{E}[XY]=44.8$ for two random variables $X$ and $Y,$ calculate the covariance of $X$ and $Y.$" :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "The covariance of $X$ and $Y$ can be calculated using the formula\n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}[X,Y]=\\text{E}[XY]-\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y].\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given values, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}[X,Y] & =\\text{E}[XY]-\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y] \\\\  & =44.8-20\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =4.8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the covariance of $X$ and $Y$ is $4.8.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162429 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162134 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fab3dcab-d386-5f54-bfba-f2e5951af9ba" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Covariance Given a Joint Probability Density Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9808b13b-2fee-56b6-a014-1a93e20b5b91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159777} {:answer/id #uuid "e0aa279a-fbf4-566c-a2e5-90c94f02f018" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159778} {:answer/id #uuid "eadf298b-3043-50fd-acb0-90abef3abd34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{e}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159779} {:answer/id #uuid "4975ae33-06ab-5386-bc3d-6d44edc8ba9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159781} {:answer/id #uuid "6f5cd552-4fe8-5f5e-92a8-327795378a43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512363}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9808b13b-2fee-56b6-a014-1a93e20b5b91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159777} :answer-field/id #uuid "316d0a76-34fa-5862-a104-987d7995c329" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159776}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3f486e7e-5dfa-501f-90c2-497028f8a357" :question/math-academy-id "q-146266" :question/problem "The random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-x-y},\\, & x>0,\\,y>0, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the covariance of $X$ and $Y.$" :question/worked-solution "The joint support of $X$ and $Y$ is given by the rectangle \n\n$$\nS=(0,\\infty )\\times (0,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nMoreover, we can write \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=g(x)\\cdot h(y),\n$$\n\nwhere $g(x)={e}^{-x}$ and $h(y)={e}^{-y}.$ \n\nTherefore, $X$ and $Y$ are independent, and consequently $\\text{Cov}[X,Y]=0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186512926 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162135 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b4549d88-dfbd-57e0-a673-99e394563613" :knowledge-point/title "Stating the Covariance Using the Definition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14139549-eab2-5905-aafa-60d90dabc834" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}(x-0.5)(y-1.6)f(x,y)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512140} {:answer/id #uuid "1513f6db-97ab-5bf7-b299-4e700eb9fc0f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}(x-1)(y-2)f(x,y)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512144} {:answer/id #uuid "8f779a44-d3e2-5a9f-8dfe-1118b2784489" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}x(y-1.6)f(x,y)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512438} {:answer/id #uuid "960ed080-6b3a-5a07-87cd-958404cfb2fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}(x-1.6)(y-0.5)f(x,y)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512453} {:answer/id #uuid "ed9ba43f-0e76-58ed-bedf-25fb75353679" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}(xy-0.5)f(x,y)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512676}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "14139549-eab2-5905-aafa-60d90dabc834" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}(x-0.5)(y-1.6)f(x,y)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512140} :answer-field/id #uuid "ce88684a-1856-52b5-9580-414ac84284b9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512837}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b1903a33-4088-5de3-962d-d8462d93f10a" :question/math-academy-id "q-147809" :question/problem "The joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ for the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ with joint support $S={S}_{X}\\times {S}_{Y}$ is given below.\n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.15$ | $0.35$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.25$ | $0.25$ |\n\nWhich of the following gives the covariance of $X$ and $Y?$" :question/worked-solution "The covariance of two discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ with joint support $S$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}[X,Y]={\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}(x-\\text{E}[X])(y-\\text{E}[Y])f(x,y).\n$$\n\nFirst, let's find the marginal mass functions for $X$ and $Y.$ These are given by the row and column totals, respectively.\n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.15$ | $0.35$ | $0.5$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.25$ | $0.25$ | $0.5$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $0.4$ | $0.6$ | $1$ |\n\nWe now compute $\\text{E}[X]$ and $\\text{E}[Y],$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\sum }_{x\\in {S}_{X}}x\\cdot {f}_{X}(x) \\\\  & =0\\cdot 0.5+1\\cdot 0.5 \\\\  & =0+0.5 \\\\  & =0.5 \\\\ \\text{E}[Y] & ={\\sum }_{y\\in {S}_{Y}}y\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y) \\\\  & =1\\cdot 0.4+2\\cdot 0.6 \\\\  & =0.4+1.2 \\\\  & =1.6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the formula for the covariance, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}[X,Y] & ={\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}(x-\\text{E}[X])(y-\\text{E}[Y])f(x,y) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}(x-0.5)(y-1.6)f(x,y).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186512941 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162134 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fab3dcab-d386-5f54-bfba-f2e5951af9ba" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Covariance Given a Joint Probability Density Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6edd5f67-1149-5905-9dfd-2531aac7d778" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{144}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512362} {:answer/id #uuid "8efe1823-faf5-5f48-bcfa-08d5910e2be9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512436} {:answer/id #uuid "9d4df0cb-ec84-5087-bbab-1841e915272d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{144}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512468} {:answer/id #uuid "caf882ed-b1ef-5c87-ab85-e0fb21914627" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{96}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512588} {:answer/id #uuid "fb927e68-a451-56b0-abb4-b479e7119a3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512706}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9d4df0cb-ec84-5087-bbab-1841e915272d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{144}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512468} :answer-field/id #uuid "d2d1682f-7eb6-5691-9d8f-0cd7e762540d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512839}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cf31f09e-0f29-56f8-9f97-abccd7a0062d" :question/math-academy-id "q-147844" :question/problem "The random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y, & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that $\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{7}{12}$ and $\\text{E}[Y]=\\frac{7}{12},$ calculate the covariance of $X$ and $Y.$" :question/worked-solution "The covariance of $X$ and $Y$ can be calculated using the formula\n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}[X,Y]=\\text{E}[XY]-\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y].\n$$\n\nTo find $\\text{E}[XY],$ we use the rule of the lazy statistician:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[XY] & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}xyf(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}xy(x+y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}y{\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{2}+xy)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}y{[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}+\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}y]}_{x=0}^{x=1}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}y[\\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{1}{2}y]\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(\\frac{1}{3}y+\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{6}{y}^{2}+\\frac{1}{6}{y}^{3}]}_{y=0}^{y=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the covariance formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}[X,Y] & =\\text{E}[XY]-\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}-(\\frac{7}{12})(\\frac{7}{12}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{144}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186512869 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162135 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b4549d88-dfbd-57e0-a673-99e394563613" :knowledge-point/title "Stating the Covariance Using the Definition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "463c0e5c-2ba7-50f8-96e8-20483d4c6b9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}(xy-0.9)f(x,y)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512245} {:answer/id #uuid "9e60445e-91ea-598a-b36b-f086786a0ad0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}y(x-2.5)f(x,y)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512470} {:answer/id #uuid "b4311664-2c93-5de9-becf-6e058c78a3f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}(x-2.5)(y-1.6)f(x,y)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512524} {:answer/id #uuid "c7bafe94-6fd3-5d6e-ab7a-2f596948d2e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}(x-2)(y-1)f(x,y)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512580} {:answer/id #uuid "cc263153-ffd5-5e1e-b113-5188544340fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}(x-1.6)(y-2.5)f(x,y)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512591}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b4311664-2c93-5de9-becf-6e058c78a3f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}(x-2.5)(y-1.6)f(x,y)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512524} :answer-field/id #uuid "2f6c5e9a-0900-5e11-9ea7-1b9d6a41d202" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512751}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0b02c01d-81c9-557d-8302-9b53cb371ef3" :question/math-academy-id "q-147919" :question/problem "The joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ for the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ with joint support $S={S}_{X}\\times {S}_{Y}$ is given below.\n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=2$ | $0.35$ | $0.4$ |\n| $X=4$ | $0.05$ | $0.2$ |\n\nWhich of the following gives the covariance of $X$ and $Y?$" :question/worked-solution "The covariance of two discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ with joint support $S$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}[X,Y]={\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}(x-\\text{E}[X])(y-\\text{E}[Y])f(x,y).\n$$\n\nFirst, let's find the marginal mass functions for $X$ and $Y.$ These are given by the row and column totals, respectively.\n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=2$ | $0.35$ | $0.4$ | $0.75$ |\n| $X=4$ | $0.05$ | $0.2$ | $0.25$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $0.4$ | $0.6$ | $1$ |\n\nWe now compute $\\text{E}[X]$ and $\\text{E}[Y],$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\sum }_{x\\in {S}_{X}}x\\cdot {f}_{X}(x) \\\\  & =2\\cdot 0.75+4\\cdot 0.25 \\\\  & =1.5+1 \\\\  & =2.5 \\\\ \\text{E}[Y] & ={\\sum }_{y\\in {S}_{Y}}y\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y) \\\\  & =1\\cdot 0.4+2\\cdot 0.6 \\\\  & =0.4+1.2 \\\\  & =1.6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the formula for the covariance, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}[X,Y] & ={\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}(x-\\text{E}[X])(y-\\text{E}[Y])f(x,y) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}(x-2.5)(y-1.6)f(x,y).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162445 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162135 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b4549d88-dfbd-57e0-a673-99e394563613" :knowledge-point/title "Stating the Covariance Using the Definition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "46aaddbb-bca6-5492-a607-bf65179003b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}x(y-1)f(x,y)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512246} {:answer/id #uuid "64951951-633f-5c92-b725-b9375ea62d0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}(xy-1.96)f(x,y)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512337} {:answer/id #uuid "b2bfb33d-f2a7-5b86-b5e6-a2e6913324fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}(x-1)(y-2)f(x,y)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512521} {:answer/id #uuid "dec1711d-2b9c-592b-9554-e3ed886ff6ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}(x-1.96)(y-3.8)f(x,y)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512635} {:answer/id #uuid "f6069bc4-f2a1-5a73-abe2-ed74bda23d86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}(x-3.8)(y-1.96)f(x,y)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512696}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dec1711d-2b9c-592b-9554-e3ed886ff6ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}(x-1.96)(y-3.8)f(x,y)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512635} :answer-field/id #uuid "ee0ffc3c-5e92-543d-a922-72f19b24c70c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159872}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "30db451b-93c6-5bae-8115-d6afd25f7fca" :question/math-academy-id "q-147920" :question/problem "The joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ for the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ with joint support $S={S}_{X}\\times {S}_{Y}$ is given below.\n\n| $f$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.12$ | $0.4$ |\n| $X=3$ | $0.28$ | $0.2$ |\n\nWhich of the following gives the covariance of $X$ and $Y?$" :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "The covariance of two discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ with joint support $S$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}[X,Y]={\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}(x-\\text{E}[X])(y-\\text{E}[Y])f(x,y).\n$$\n\nFirst, let's find the marginal mass functions for $X$ and $Y.$ These are given by the row and column totals, respectively.\n\n| $f$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=5$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.12$ | $0.4$ | $0.52$ |\n| $X=3$ | $0.28$ | $0.2$ | $0.48$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $0.4$ | $0.6$ | $1$ |\n\nWe now compute $\\text{E}[X]$ and $\\text{E}[Y],$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\sum }_{x\\in {S}_{X}}x\\cdot {f}_{X}(x) \\\\  & =1\\cdot 0.52+3\\cdot 0.48 \\\\  & =0.52+1.44 \\\\  & =1.96 \\\\ \\text{E}[Y] & ={\\sum }_{y\\in {S}_{Y}}y\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y) \\\\  & =2\\cdot 0.4+5\\cdot 0.6 \\\\  & =0.8+3 \\\\  & =3.8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the formula for the covariance, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}[X,Y] & ={\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}(x-\\text{E}[X])(y-\\text{E}[Y])f(x,y) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}(x-1.96)(y-3.8)f(x,y).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186512952 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162135 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b4549d88-dfbd-57e0-a673-99e394563613" :knowledge-point/title "Stating the Covariance Using the Definition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9a1a2a02-2456-5c73-acbf-e95158980052" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}(x-4)(y-3)f(x,y)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512463} {:answer/id #uuid "c4cede03-6baa-574c-a7c4-ebb828929447" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}(x-3.9)(y-3.2)f(x,y)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512573} {:answer/id #uuid "d17c957f-7117-5e98-a9d4-19630ec78772" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}(x-3.2)(y-3.9)f(x,y)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512600} {:answer/id #uuid "e120f5f5-62c9-5f28-b399-3c892b4d769c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}x(y-3)f(x,y)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512641} {:answer/id #uuid "ebfe97bf-65ea-59c0-a75e-fdeed2ff85a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}(xy-3)f(x,y)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512668}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c4cede03-6baa-574c-a7c4-ebb828929447" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}(x-3.9)(y-3.2)f(x,y)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512573} :answer-field/id #uuid "b38d90bb-799a-5c24-8952-a9192763487d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512819}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ef29076a-1f6b-53fd-9d0b-390107f2fcd7" :question/math-academy-id "q-147922" :question/problem "The joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ for the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ with joint support $S={S}_{X}\\times {S}_{Y}$ is given below.\n\n| $f$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=2$ | $0.15$ | $0.1$ |\n| $X=4$ | $0.2$ | $0.35$ |\n| $X=6$ | $0.05$ | $0.15$ |\n\nWhich of the following gives the covariance of $X$ and $Y?$" :question/worked-solution "The covariance of two discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ with joint support $S$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}[X,Y]={\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}(x-\\text{E}[X])(y-\\text{E}[Y])f(x,y).\n$$\n\nFirst, let's find the marginal mass functions for $X$ and $Y.$ These are given by the row and column totals, respectively.\n\n| $f$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=2$ | $0.15$ | $0.1$ | $0.25$ |\n| $X=4$ | $0.2$ | $0.35$ | $0.55$ |\n| $X=6$ | $0.05$ | $0.15$ | $0.2$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $0.4$ | $0.6$ | $1$ |\n\nWe now compute $\\text{E}[X]$ and $\\text{E}[Y],$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\sum }_{x\\in {S}_{X}}x\\cdot {f}_{X}(x) \\\\  & =2\\cdot 0.25+4\\cdot 0.55+6\\cdot 0.2 \\\\  & =0.5+2.2+1.2 \\\\  & =3.9 \\\\ \\text{E}[Y] & ={\\sum }_{y\\in {S}_{Y}}y\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y) \\\\  & =2\\cdot 0.4+4\\cdot 0.6 \\\\  & =0.8+2.4 \\\\  & =3.2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the formula for the covariance, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}[X,Y] & ={\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}(x-\\text{E}[X])(y-\\text{E}[Y])f(x,y) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}(x-3.9)(y-3.2)f(x,y).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186512899 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162135 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b4549d88-dfbd-57e0-a673-99e394563613" :knowledge-point/title "Stating the Covariance Using the Definition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5b1d773b-d4bb-59c7-830e-2a801507e0f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}y(x-3)f(x,y)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512310} {:answer/id #uuid "78d9bb9c-a88b-5fd8-b931-84bb41627aeb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}(x-3.2)(y-3)f(x,y)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512383} {:answer/id #uuid "baf3b981-1b24-5859-8dba-d16fd4d8d6d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}(xy-3)f(x,y)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512548} {:answer/id #uuid "d33db9bc-7f32-5a64-8e28-bd38babbfb73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}(xy-6.2)f(x,y)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512603} {:answer/id #uuid "d83ebf83-a6a9-5845-be10-a3c5854de0b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}(x-3)(y-3.2)f(x,y)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512616}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d83ebf83-a6a9-5845-be10-a3c5854de0b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}(x-3)(y-3.2)f(x,y)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512616} :answer-field/id #uuid "1543b923-1e80-5eb5-8e96-fc9f0590c038" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512735}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7601220c-590a-55f7-9ebc-4ae99b2759bd" :question/math-academy-id "q-147925" :question/problem "The joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ for the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ with joint support $S={S}_{X}\\times {S}_{Y}$ is given below.\n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=3$ | $Y=5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=2$ | $0.1$ | $0.12$ | $0.28$ |\n| $X=4$ | $0.2$ | $0.18$ | $0.12$ |\n\nWhich of the following gives the covariance of $X$ and $Y?$" :question/worked-solution "The covariance of two discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ with joint support $S$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}[X,Y]={\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}(x-\\text{E}[X])(y-\\text{E}[Y])f(x,y).\n$$\n\nFirst, let's find the marginal mass functions for $X$ and $Y.$ These are given by the row and column totals, respectively.\n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=3$ | $Y=5$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=2$ | $0.1$ | $0.12$ | $0.28$ | $0.5$ |\n| $X=4$ | $0.2$ | $0.18$ | $0.12$ | $0.5$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $0.3$ | $0.3$ | $0.4$ | $1$ |\n\nWe now compute $\\text{E}[X]$ and $\\text{E}[Y],$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\sum }_{x\\in {S}_{X}}x\\cdot {f}_{X}(x) \\\\  & =2\\cdot 0.5+4\\cdot 0.5 \\\\  & =1+2 \\\\  & =3 \\\\ \\text{E}[Y] & ={\\sum }_{y\\in {S}_{Y}}y\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y) \\\\  & =1\\cdot 0.3+3\\cdot 0.3+5\\cdot 0.4 \\\\  & =0.3+0.9+2 \\\\  & =3.2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the formula for the covariance, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}[X,Y] & ={\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}(x-\\text{E}[X])(y-\\text{E}[Y])f(x,y) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}(x-3)(y-3.2)f(x,y).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186512888 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162134 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fab3dcab-d386-5f54-bfba-f2e5951af9ba" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Covariance Given a Joint Probability Density Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8a36bbdb-d7de-52bd-851d-e6bd6d33739c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512424} {:answer/id #uuid "a49377ee-551e-5cb2-a025-28a2082dd9a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{161}{100}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512487} {:answer/id #uuid "d4c9bf09-d22c-5175-8478-b7129d7b3be1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{9}{100}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512605} {:answer/id #uuid "d5d6b444-7189-5948-8da8-571f44e98958" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512607} {:answer/id #uuid "ee2b176c-6cdb-59e7-ad44-08efb439d9ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512678}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d4c9bf09-d22c-5175-8478-b7129d7b3be1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{9}{100}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512605} :answer-field/id #uuid "df1e1d9e-0dc1-5725-b77d-a7edfadad3f3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512848}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "57775fd5-4d0c-5406-bb3e-6af6db58e9c9" :question/math-academy-id "q-147945" :question/problem "The random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{16}({x}^{3}+{y}^{3}),\\, & 0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 2, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that $\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{13}{10}$ and $\\text{E}[Y]=\\frac{13}{10},$ calculate the covariance of $X$ and $Y.$" :question/worked-solution "The covariance of $X$ and $Y$ can be calculated using the formula\n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}[X,Y]=\\text{E}[XY]-\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y].\n$$\n\nTo find $\\text{E}[XY],$ we use the rule of the lazy statistician:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[XY] & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}xyf(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}xy\\cdot \\frac{1}{16}({x}^{3}+{y}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{16}y{\\int }_{0}^{2}({x}^{4}+x{y}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{16}y{[\\frac{1}{5}{x}^{5}+\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}{y}^{3}]}_{x=0}^{x=2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{16}y[\\frac{32}{5}+2{y}^{3}]\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(\\frac{2}{5}y+\\frac{1}{8}{y}^{4})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{5}{y}^{2}+\\frac{1}{40}{y}^{5}]}_{y=0}^{y=2} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the covariance formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}[X,Y] & =\\text{E}[XY]-\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y] \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{5}-(\\frac{13}{10})(\\frac{13}{10}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{9}{100}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186411854 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162134 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fab3dcab-d386-5f54-bfba-f2e5951af9ba" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Covariance Given a Joint Probability Density Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "964c5bc4-7a2e-5bae-85a7-d482c6e36e48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411756} {:answer/id #uuid "a758ee1c-9dab-5058-8a43-ffb91581708b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411765} {:answer/id #uuid "c3bca5a5-b1a9-54bd-8c07-941077c325cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{17}{32}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411785} {:answer/id #uuid "e2b6fede-844a-5216-ae74-664077e8f2bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{64}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411805} {:answer/id #uuid "f1b661e8-65e7-5407-8292-c4496fc2965b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411812}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e2b6fede-844a-5216-ae74-664077e8f2bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{64}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411805} :answer-field/id #uuid "dee10a7b-d9ae-5a81-b136-732cb3456d2f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411847}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1994bb13-7165-5891-a83f-5e7560b1da72" :question/math-academy-id "q-147946" :question/problem "The random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{8}(x+{y}^{2}),\\, & 0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that $\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{5}{4}$ and $\\text{E}[Y]=\\frac{9}{16},$ calculate the covariance of $X$ and $Y.$" :question/worked-solution "The covariance of $X$ and $Y$ can be calculated using the formula\n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}[X,Y]=\\text{E}[XY]-\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y].\n$$\n\nTo find $\\text{E}[XY],$ we use the rule of the lazy statistician:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[XY] & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}xyf(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}xy\\cdot \\frac{3}{8}(x+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{3}{8}y{\\int }_{0}^{2}({x}^{2}+x{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{3}{8}y{[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}+\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}{y}^{2}]}_{x=0}^{x=2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{3}{8}y[\\frac{8}{3}+2{y}^{2}]\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(y+\\frac{3}{4}{y}^{3})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}+\\frac{3}{16}{y}^{4}]}_{y=0}^{y=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{16}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the covariance formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}[X,Y] & =\\text{E}[XY]-\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y] \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{16}-(\\frac{5}{4})(\\frac{9}{16}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{64}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186512880 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162134 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fab3dcab-d386-5f54-bfba-f2e5951af9ba" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Covariance Given a Joint Probability Density Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00c23a39-a692-59f0-82d6-1e42aa201914" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{214}{125}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512098} {:answer/id #uuid "587f7451-fccf-5637-a502-7b906ce3c5c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512303} {:answer/id #uuid "5c47d0b3-930f-5e0f-872b-04d2b1a8ab8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512313} {:answer/id #uuid "a7f54150-f261-5643-bee1-64de82d8bd4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{52}{75}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512499} {:answer/id #uuid "b96bcde9-98d4-501d-9658-acfed2d6a463" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{125}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512545}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b96bcde9-98d4-501d-9658-acfed2d6a463" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{125}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512545} :answer-field/id #uuid "0c5eaee8-55ac-56b1-9f8a-3b273fc778c6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512728}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "28314126-6eaa-5326-a420-9e962fb3a315" :question/math-academy-id "q-147950" :question/problem "The random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{5}({x}^{3}+y),\\, & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 2, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that $\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{14}{25}$ and $\\text{E}[Y]=\\frac{19}{15},$ calculate the covariance of $X$ and $Y.$" :question/worked-solution "The covariance of $X$ and $Y$ can be calculated using the formula\n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}[X,Y]=\\text{E}[XY]-\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y].\n$$\n\nTo find $\\text{E}[XY],$ we use the rule of the lazy statistician:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[XY] & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}xyf(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}xy\\cdot \\frac{2}{5}({x}^{3}+y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{2}{5}y{\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{4}+xy)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{2}{5}y{[\\frac{1}{5}{x}^{5}+\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}y]}_{x=0}^{x=1}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{2}{5}y[\\frac{1}{5}+\\frac{1}{2}y]\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(\\frac{2}{25}y+\\frac{1}{5}{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{25}{y}^{2}+\\frac{1}{15}{y}^{3}]}_{y=0}^{y=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{52}{75}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the covariance formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}[X,Y] & =\\text{E}[XY]-\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y] \\\\  & =\\frac{52}{75}-(\\frac{14}{25})(\\frac{19}{15}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{125}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186512905 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162132 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "130d80d7-d0f9-5979-b966-e6c0bf7a27e9" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Covariance Using the Definition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "142f00ef-98a1-5d96-923f-8c06a4dafd48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512141} {:answer/id #uuid "205120df-f97d-504e-8f59-c17c4b4fa683" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512167} {:answer/id #uuid "83ff5871-6f27-5a5e-9a5a-cfcf1a804151" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512406} {:answer/id #uuid "92f5bc33-1122-5445-b18c-128cf3c6fad5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512447} {:answer/id #uuid "b0d883f9-65cd-5210-a239-f5446174972c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.02" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512515}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "83ff5871-6f27-5a5e-9a5a-cfcf1a804151" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512406} :answer-field/id #uuid "6210317b-2bf1-5300-979a-28521cef14d8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512780}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "88c40e55-9afb-513d-8399-c6e943bf9ded" :question/math-academy-id "q-147964" :question/problem "The joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ for the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given below.\n\n| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.05$ | $0.2$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.15$ | $0.6$ |\n\nCalculate the covariance of $X$ and $Y.$\n\n*Hint: It can be shown that $P(X=x,Y=y)=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible values of $x$ and $y.$*" :question/worked-solution "The covariance of two discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ with joint support $S$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}[X,Y]={\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}(x-\\text{E}[X])(y-\\text{E}[Y])f(x,y).\n$$\n\nWe're told that\n\n$$\nP(X=x,Y=y)=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)\n$$\n\nfor all possible values of $x$ and $y.$ Therefore, $X$ and $Y$ are independent. \n\nSince $X$ are $Y$ are independent, we have $\\text{Cov}(X,Y)=0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186512918 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162132 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "130d80d7-d0f9-5979-b966-e6c0bf7a27e9" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Covariance Using the Definition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a605469-14f1-547a-a954-a026a62f884f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512196} {:answer/id #uuid "375d7ff0-fa73-535c-b7b2-882d3c449c47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512222} {:answer/id #uuid "c2a22f44-f278-57d8-bf67-af4a421c8db7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512564} {:answer/id #uuid "dab5d621-8844-5673-8184-cb03e682f420" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512620} {:answer/id #uuid "f8889368-331a-5a5c-a70e-2170551b3d70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512700}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dab5d621-8844-5673-8184-cb03e682f420" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512620} :answer-field/id #uuid "5afcdbc9-8272-5f52-8b74-ad215de0627c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512775}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a725de9b-9a65-5d96-80a3-b82e15275c01" :question/math-academy-id "q-147967" :question/problem "The joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ for the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given below.\n\n| $f$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.5$ | $0$ |\n| $X=3$ | $0.2$ | $0.3$ |\n\nCalculate the covariance of $X$ and $Y.$" :question/worked-solution "The covariance of two discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ with joint support $S$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}[X,Y]={\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}(x-\\text{E}[X])(y-\\text{E}[Y])f(x,y).\n$$\n\nFirst, let's find the marginal mass functions for $X$ and $Y.$ These are given by the row and column totals, respectively.\n\n| $f$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.5$ | $0$ | $0.5$ |\n| $X=3$ | $0.2$ | $0.3$ | $0.5$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $0.7$ | $0.3$ | $1$ |\n\nWe now compute $\\text{E}[X]$ and $\\text{E}[Y],$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\sum }_{x\\in {S}_{X}}x\\cdot {f}_{X}(x) \\\\  & =1\\cdot 0.5+3\\cdot 0.5 \\\\  & =0.5+1.5 \\\\  & =2 \\\\ \\text{E}[Y] & ={\\sum }_{y\\in {S}_{Y}}y\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y) \\\\  & =2\\cdot 0.7+4\\cdot 0.3 \\\\  & =1.4+1.2 \\\\  & =2.6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the formula for the covariance, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}[X,Y] & ={\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}(x-\\text{E}[X])(y-\\text{E}[Y])f(x,y) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}(x-2)(y-2.6)f(x,y) \\\\  & =(1-2)(2-2.6)f(1,2) \\\\  & +(1-2)(4-2.6)f(1,4) \\\\  & +(3-2)(2-2.6)f(3,2) \\\\  & +(3-2)(4-2.6)f(3,4) \\\\  & =(-1)(-0.6)(0.5) \\\\  & +(-1)(1.4)(0) \\\\  & +(1)(-0.6)(0.2) \\\\  & +(1)(1.4)(0.3) \\\\  & =0.6.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186512882 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162132 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "130d80d7-d0f9-5979-b966-e6c0bf7a27e9" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Covariance Using the Definition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0237c166-3356-51c7-8d41-e5ff9c1a41a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.39" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512103} {:answer/id #uuid "1be00930-3e28-5e0c-a0b5-2a488dcdde31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.17" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512159} {:answer/id #uuid "99cf3385-7261-5684-96b3-853497b12cef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.23" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512461} {:answer/id #uuid "a695d0e9-7192-58ec-8052-80f798ee38f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.57" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512495} {:answer/id #uuid "afade78c-7daa-53c1-9c28-a61cf8c12286" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512511}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0237c166-3356-51c7-8d41-e5ff9c1a41a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.39" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512103} :answer-field/id #uuid "1e0828f6-c287-56e0-916a-4821803b818a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512739}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2ce015c9-6f9e-5825-a2d1-d00ea38bdb08" :question/math-academy-id "q-147968" :question/problem "The joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ for the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given below.\n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.1$ | $0.25$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0$ | $0.65$ |\n\nCalculate the covariance of $X$ and $Y.$" :question/worked-solution "The covariance of two discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ with joint support $S$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}[X,Y]={\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}(x-\\text{E}[X])(y-\\text{E}[Y])f(x,y).\n$$\n\nFirst, let's find the marginal mass functions for $X$ and $Y.$ These are given by the row and column totals, respectively.\n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=4$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.1$ | $0.25$ | $0.35$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0$ | $0.65$ | $0.65$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $0.1$ | $0.9$ | $1$ |\n\nWe now compute $\\text{E}[X]$ and $\\text{E}[Y],$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\sum }_{x\\in {S}_{X}}x\\cdot {f}_{X}(x) \\\\  & =0\\cdot 0.35+2\\cdot 0.65 \\\\  & =0+1.3 \\\\  & =1.3 \\\\ \\text{E}[Y] & ={\\sum }_{y\\in {S}_{Y}}y\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y) \\\\  & =1\\cdot 0.1+4\\cdot 0.9 \\\\  & =0.1+3.6 \\\\  & =3.7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the formula for the covariance, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}[X,Y] & ={\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}(x-\\text{E}[X])(y-\\text{E}[Y])f(x,y) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}(x-1.3)(y-3.7)f(x,y) \\\\  & =(0-1.3)(1-3.7)f(0,1) \\\\  & +(0-1.3)(4-3.7)f(0,4) \\\\  & +(2-1.3)(1-3.7)f(2,1) \\\\  & +(2-1.3)(4-3.7)f(2,4) \\\\  & =(-1.3)(-2.7)(0.1) \\\\  & +(-1.3)(0.3)(0.25) \\\\  & +(0.7)(-2.7)(0) \\\\  & +(0.7)(0.3)(0.65) \\\\  & =0.39.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186512944 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162132 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "130d80d7-d0f9-5979-b966-e6c0bf7a27e9" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Covariance Using the Definition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "371679c2-2b5e-5e2c-aee9-30b820dc41f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512221} {:answer/id #uuid "4b3ee59b-1cd4-5037-ae30-111664dd5bf5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.08" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512259} {:answer/id #uuid "55a06749-2d40-522b-a303-cd5f186203c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.23" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512292} {:answer/id #uuid "6031512a-ed66-5a1d-baeb-1e186681d531" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512328} {:answer/id #uuid "8924f8e7-ffa9-5f5c-a566-8747fbe8e0e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.02" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512419}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8924f8e7-ffa9-5f5c-a566-8747fbe8e0e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.02" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512419} :answer-field/id #uuid "811156d6-65a9-5f35-a8ae-1aca43ee3f12" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512797}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d4d126ea-cebf-548f-a0ce-ca7561957246" :question/math-academy-id "q-147970" :question/problem "The joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ for the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given below.\n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=2$ | $0.3$ | $0.1$ |\n| $X=3$ | $0.4$ | $0.2$ |\n\nCalculate the covariance of $X$ and $Y.$" :question/worked-solution "The covariance of two discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ with joint support $S$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}[X,Y]={\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}(x-\\text{E}[X])(y-\\text{E}[Y])f(x,y).\n$$\n\nFirst, let's find the marginal mass functions for $X$ and $Y.$ These are given by the row and column totals, respectively.\n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=2$ | $0.3$ | $0.1$ | $0.4$ |\n| $X=3$ | $0.4$ | $0.2$ | $0.6$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $0.7$ | $0.3$ | $1$ |\n\nWe now compute $\\text{E}[X]$ and $\\text{E}[Y],$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\sum }_{x\\in {S}_{X}}x\\cdot {f}_{X}(x) \\\\  & =2\\cdot 0.4+3\\cdot 0.6 \\\\  & =0.8+1.8 \\\\  & =2.6 \\\\ \\text{E}[Y] & ={\\sum }_{y\\in {S}_{Y}}y\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y) \\\\  & =1\\cdot 0.7+2\\cdot 0.3 \\\\  & =0.7+0.6 \\\\  & =1.3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the formula for the covariance, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}[X,Y] & ={\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}(x-\\text{E}[X])(y-\\text{E}[Y])f(x,y) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}(x-2.6)(y-1.3)f(x,y) \\\\  & =(2-2.6)(1-1.3)f(2,1) \\\\  & +(2-2.6)(2-1.3)f(2,2) \\\\  & +(3-2.6)(1-1.3)f(3,1) \\\\  & +(3-2.6)(2-1.3)f(3,2) \\\\  & =(-0.6)(-0.3)(0.3) \\\\  & +(-0.6)(0.7)(0.1) \\\\  & +(0.4)(-0.3)(0.4) \\\\  & +(0.4)(0.7)(0.2) \\\\  & =0.02.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186512897 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162132 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "130d80d7-d0f9-5979-b966-e6c0bf7a27e9" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Covariance Using the Definition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5054ca35-1983-54f9-8a67-129a18df5cf4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.26" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512276} {:answer/id #uuid "6290de49-ff0a-5e48-8570-362804720050" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.44" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512333} {:answer/id #uuid "94764131-66fd-56ec-b6a6-08e292c7818e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512449} {:answer/id #uuid "b9321fe8-9a74-5033-a5e9-d9d7066c5ed1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512542} {:answer/id #uuid "e45bf0f5-e0ae-5592-aa27-6e370b6c4f78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.38" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512645}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6290de49-ff0a-5e48-8570-362804720050" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.44" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512333} :answer-field/id #uuid "e318cf23-99c3-5de3-b262-09a09b316069" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512851}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "72eb6c64-1cf3-5dde-b025-69a7158cf18b" :question/math-academy-id "q-147971" :question/problem "The joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ for the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given below.\n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.15$ | $0.25$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.5$ | $0.1$ |\n\nCalculate the covariance of $X$ and $Y.$" :question/worked-solution "The covariance of two discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ with joint support $S$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}[X,Y]={\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}(x-\\text{E}[X])(y-\\text{E}[Y])f(x,y).\n$$\n\nFirst, let's find the marginal mass functions for $X$ and $Y.$ These are given by the row and column totals, respectively.\n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=3$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.15$ | $0.25$ | $0.4$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.5$ | $0.1$ | $0.6$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $0.65$ | $0.35$ | $1$ |\n\nWe now compute $\\text{E}[X]$ and $\\text{E}[Y],$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\sum }_{x\\in {S}_{X}}x\\cdot {f}_{X}(x) \\\\  & =0\\cdot 0.4+2\\cdot 0.6 \\\\  & =0+1.2 \\\\  & =1.2 \\\\ \\text{E}[Y] & ={\\sum }_{y\\in {S}_{Y}}y\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y) \\\\  & =1\\cdot 0.65+3\\cdot 0.35 \\\\  & =0.65+1.05 \\\\  & =1.7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the formula for the covariance, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}[X,Y] & ={\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}(x-\\text{E}[X])(y-\\text{E}[Y])f(x,y) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}(x-1.2)(y-1.7)f(x,y) \\\\  & =(0-1.2)(1-1.7)f(0,1) \\\\  & +(0-1.2)(3-1.7)f(0,3) \\\\  & +(2-1.2)(1-1.7)f(2,1) \\\\  & +(2-1.2)(3-1.7)f(2,3) \\\\  & =(-1.2)(-0.7)(0.15) \\\\  & +(-1.2)(1.3)(0.25) \\\\  & +(0.8)(-0.7)(0.5) \\\\  & +(0.8)(1.3)(0.1) \\\\  & =-0.44.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186512959 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162136 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "929a4b02-6c3d-59ce-b774-7ca6487077ff" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Covariance Using the Shortcut Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "54d258a4-8ebf-51a7-a775-2aba72b3518a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512291} {:answer/id #uuid "75bec082-0e2e-5a44-bf42-16ad67606664" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512377} {:answer/id #uuid "bc4512a9-45d3-53d4-9436-13626851cb5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.42" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512550} {:answer/id #uuid "bcce625e-1d39-516d-a209-5a72ac27a373" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512551} {:answer/id #uuid "c3490969-2466-5c09-b71b-7b9702da6997" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512566}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "54d258a4-8ebf-51a7-a775-2aba72b3518a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512291} :answer-field/id #uuid "6c475b4b-06c7-52f7-8d6e-71a8a2f19ded" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512785}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fefbc176-d8f3-53d4-bb24-386b85087084" :question/math-academy-id "q-148014" :question/problem "If $\\text{E}[X]=5.2,$ $\\text{E}[Y]=4.2,$ and $\\text{E}[XY]=22$ for two random variables $X$ and $Y,$ calculate the covariance of $X$ and $Y.$" :question/worked-solution "The covariance of $X$ and $Y$ can be calculated using the formula\n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}[X,Y]=\\text{E}[XY]-\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y].\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given values, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}[X,Y] & =\\text{E}[XY]-\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y] \\\\  & =22-(5.2)\\cdot (4.2) \\\\  & =0.16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the covariance of $X$ and $Y$ is $0.16.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186512912 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162136 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "929a4b02-6c3d-59ce-b774-7ca6487077ff" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Covariance Using the Shortcut Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a68ae83-4e32-50f6-a16e-5467eb325b33" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.06" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512197} {:answer/id #uuid "5ea5a9f6-1000-5073-8452-d449754e937c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.02" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512324} {:answer/id #uuid "783f33c0-deac-509b-8860-a758465241bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.17" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512382} {:answer/id #uuid "ebb3475e-596a-53ca-a088-db2e7f5abce7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512666} {:answer/id #uuid "edf7be1a-0847-520d-a68d-210de044d15a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512677}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "783f33c0-deac-509b-8860-a758465241bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.17" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512382} :answer-field/id #uuid "5e9bc202-ef39-51ee-b9b1-9f179e2aa12e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512777}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9576e0da-b7f3-5620-ad1a-43d5569461f3" :question/math-academy-id "q-148027" :question/problem "The joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ for the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given below.\n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.15$ | $0.2$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.4$ | $0.25$ |\n\nIf $\\text{E}[X]=1.3$ and $\\text{E}[Y]=1.9,$ calculate the covariance of $X$ and $Y.$" :question/worked-solution "The covariance of $X$ and $Y$ can be calculated using the formula\n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}[X,Y]=\\text{E}[XY]-\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y].\n$$\n\nWe use the rule of the lazy statistician to find $\\text{E}[XY]:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[XY] & ={\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}xy\\cdot f(x,y) \\\\  & =(0)(1)(0.15)+(0)(3)(0.2)+(2)(1)(0.4)+(2)(3)(0.25) \\\\  & =2.3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the covariance formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}[X,Y] & =\\text{E}[XY]-\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y] \\\\  & =2.3-(1.3)(1.9) \\\\  & =-0.17.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186512946 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162136 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "929a4b02-6c3d-59ce-b774-7ca6487077ff" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Covariance Using the Shortcut Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07ef0ca5-25f0-5fa7-8ba9-189382bdbf81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512121} {:answer/id #uuid "2e6403bf-0c0f-5722-a905-d4b7937789ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.08" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512204} {:answer/id #uuid "3e134d87-91b5-59ee-9fa9-8526a1584916" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512233} {:answer/id #uuid "5c85b8f8-8638-554c-8039-45a2e66a8c10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512314} {:answer/id #uuid "873920de-2222-59b9-88f0-66b71c16c424" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.04" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512412}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "873920de-2222-59b9-88f0-66b71c16c424" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.04" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512412} :answer-field/id #uuid "ce8c62ae-2570-57ee-ab84-4a3dc6da3175" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512838}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "de144ac2-d89b-5e69-8e47-de2554ce330e" :question/math-academy-id "q-148028" :question/problem "The joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ for the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given below.\n\n| $f$ | $Y=3$ | $Y=5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=2$ | $0.25$ | $0.15$ |\n| $X=4$ | $0.35$ | $0.25$ |\n\nIf $\\text{E}[X]=3.2$ and $\\text{E}[Y]=3.8,$ calculate the covariance of $X$ and $Y.$" :question/worked-solution "The covariance of $X$ and $Y$ can be calculated using the formula\n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}[X,Y]=\\text{E}[XY]-\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y].\n$$\n\nWe use the rule of the lazy statistician to find $\\text{E}[XY]:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[XY] & ={\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}xy\\cdot f(x,y) \\\\  & =(2)(3)(0.25)+(2)(5)(0.15)+(4)(3)(0.35)+(4)(5)(0.25) \\\\  & =12.2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the covariance formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}[X,Y] & =\\text{E}[XY]-\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y] \\\\  & =12.2-(3.2)(3.8) \\\\  & =0.04.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186512928 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162136 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "929a4b02-6c3d-59ce-b774-7ca6487077ff" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Covariance Using the Shortcut Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3309982c-a8e1-5289-81aa-260983631647" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512210} {:answer/id #uuid "3ee2ecab-b07c-54f2-bc92-ac62bef82687" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512234} {:answer/id #uuid "57eb2365-78bc-5b7f-80bb-17bad2196177" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512300} {:answer/id #uuid "bd05d92c-95ee-535e-ba58-0ce2922a4501" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512553} {:answer/id #uuid "dfeb9861-b71c-5185-9816-b52111412339" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512639}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dfeb9861-b71c-5185-9816-b52111412339" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512639} :answer-field/id #uuid "042ea3ff-f58a-51d0-9dff-1a3e79511b55" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512724}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b781bcca-e045-541a-9fb8-bd56d31a763e" :question/math-academy-id "q-148030" :question/problem "The joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ for the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given below.\n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=2$ | $0.2$ | $0.1$ |\n| $X=4$ | $0.2$ | $0.2$ |\n| $X=6$ | $0.2$ | $0.1$ |\n\nIf $\\text{E}[X]=4$ and $\\text{E}[Y]=1.4,$ calculate the covariance of $X$ and $Y.$" :question/worked-solution "The covariance of $X$ and $Y$ can be calculated using the formula\n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}[X,Y]=\\text{E}[XY]-\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y].\n$$\n\nWe use the rule of the lazy statistician to find $\\text{E}[XY]:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[XY] & ={\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}xy\\cdot f(x,y) \\\\  & =(2)(1)(0.2)+(2)(2)(0.1)+(4)(1)(0.2) \\\\  & +(4)(2)(0.2)+(6)(1)(0.2)+(6)(2)(0.1) \\\\  & =5.6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the covariance formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}[X,Y] & =\\text{E}[XY]-\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y] \\\\  & =5.6-(4)(1.4) \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
